      "sample_type": "SERUM",
      "method": "Slide agglutination based assay",
      "interpretation": "Widal test is a serological test and is used for the diagnosis of enteric fever or typhoid fever. It is an agglutination test in which specific typhoid fever antibodies are detected by mixing the patient's serum with killed bacterial suspension of Salmonella carrying specific O, H, AH and BH antigens and observed for clumping ie. Antigen-antibody reaction. The main principle of Widal test is that if homologous antibody is present in patient's serum, it will react with respective antigen in the suspension and gives visible clumping on the test slide or card.",
